---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../data/site";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Organizational Tools Disclaimer | Caring for Aging Parents"
  description="Important notice: Caring for Aging Parents provides plain-paper organizational tools only, not medical, legal, or financial advice."
  canonicalPath="/disclaimer/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Disclaimer", href: "/disclaimer/" }]}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="prose-measure space-y-8">
      <h1 class="font-serif text-teal">
        Organizational tools disclaimer
      </h1>

      <div class="rounded-xl border-2 border-brown bg-cream p-6">
        <p class="font-bold text-ink">
          {siteConfig.disclaimerText}
        </p>
      </div>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-teal">
          1. Strictly organizational and household logistics tools
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink">
          Everything published on <strong>{siteConfig.name}</strong>—including our printable PDF sheets, free sample page, and written guides—is provided solely to help families organize everyday household routines, phone lists, visitor handovers, and physical item locations.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-teal">
          2. Not medical, legal, or financial advice
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink">
          We are not doctors, nurses, lawyers, financial planners, or professional care managers. Nothing on this website or in our printable PDFs should be taken as medical advice, legal counsel, or financial guidance. Always speak with a qualified professional in your area regarding questions about health, legal documents, or finances.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-teal">
          3. Keep passwords and account numbers off paper
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink">
          Our sheets are designed to sit on a kitchen counter, clipboard, or household binder so family members can coordinate daily tasks. For your family's safety, never write passwords, passcodes, PINs, Social Security numbers, or financial account numbers on printed worksheets. Write only physical household locations (such as which room or file drawer holds a folder) and company names.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-teal">
          4. Questions
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink">
          If you have any questions about this disclaimer, please reach out to us at <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
